ormation it collects, with whom the data is shared, and how users can control the use of their personal information.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="156547">privacy statement</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2773851">заява аб канфідэнцыяльнасці</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10398_307432_2107782"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The policy tool that gives authors control over how recipients use the documents and emails they send.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="307432">Information Rights Management</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2107782">IRM</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10398_307432_2763182"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The policy tool that gives authors control over how recipients use the documents and emails they send.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="307432">Information Rights Management</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2763182">Кіраванне правамі на доступ да інфармацыі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10398_307472_2107782"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The policy tool that gives authors control over how recipients use the documents and emails they send.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="307472">IRM</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2107782">IRM</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10398_307472_2763182"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The policy tool that gives authors control over how recipients use the documents and emails they send.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="307472">IRM</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2763182">Кіраванне правамі на доступ да інфармацыі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1040_378778_2296665"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A parameter that does not take an argument.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="378778">switch parameter</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296665">параметр-пераключальнік</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10402_146400_1860272"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Text or some other element used in an application as an indicator that the user should enter in his or her own text.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="146400">placeholder text</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1860272">замяшчальны тэкст</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10410_397225_2296226"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Text that is added to email messages in transport to provide information that supports the sending organization's compliance policies, warnings about unknown or unverified email senders, or other information as determined by the sending organization. Exchange Server 2007 allows the administrator to use transport rules to target disclaimers based on specific criteria.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="397225">disclaimer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296226">заява аб абмежаванні адказнасці</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10414_270278_1864537"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A line that separates the numerator and denominator of a fraction.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="270278">fraction bar</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864537">дробавая рыса</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10421_210482_1864401"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A small space on the To-Do Bar where the user can input tasks directly. The default label reads "Type a new task".</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="210482">task input panel</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864401">панэль уводу задач</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10423_232516_1806276"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Data from a table, form, query, view, or stored procedure, displayed in a row-and-column format.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="232516">datasheet</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1806276">табліца дадзеных</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10425_77712_2296449"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A highspeed network that can carry voice, data, and images at up to 200 Mbps or faster over distances of up to 75 km. Based on the network architecture, the transmission speed can be higher for shorter distances. A MAN, which can include one or more LANs as well as telecommunications equipment such as microwave and satellite relay stations, is smaller than a wide area network but generally operates at a higher speed.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="77712">MAN</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296449">гарадская сетка</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10425_77713_2296449"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A highspeed network that can carry voice, data, and images at up to 200 Mbps or faster over distances of up to 75 km. Based on the network architecture, the transmission speed can be higher for shorter distances. A MAN, which can include one or more LANs as well as telecommunications equipment such as microwave and satellite relay stations, is smaller than a wide area network but generally operates at a higher speed.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="77713">metropolitan area network</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296449">гарадская сетка</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10431_232847_1860362"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A view that is designed for reading documents on a computer screen. The document is resized to fit the screen and most toolbars are removed, but commands are available for navigating, commenting, and looking up words.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="232847">reading layout view</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1860362">рэжым чытання</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10436_415517_1864588"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Editor feature that gives users feedback on how easy it is for a reader to understand a written text based on information such as average sentence length and average word length.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="415517">Readability Statistics</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864588">статыстыка лёгкачытальнасці</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10437_168488_1864352"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An optional Live Meeting tool that allows users to create Live Meeting slides and add a presenter photo as part of a Microsoft PowerPoint file.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="168488">PowerPoint add-in</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864352">надбудова PowerPoint</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10443_294444_1864542"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of chart that compares the aggregate values of a number of data series.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="294444">radar chart</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864542">пялёсткавая дыяграма</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10444_139402_1864223"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A design template that also contains text suggestions on each slide. You replace the text suggestions with the text that you want. A content template contains a slide master and an optional title master.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="139402">content template</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864223">шаблон змесціва</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1045_137287_1780195"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Text displayed by Web browsers during image downloads for users who have graphics turned off, and for users who rely on screen-reading software to convert graphics on the screen to spoken words.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="137287">alternative text</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1780195">тэкст замяшчэння</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1045_137287_1806241"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Text displayed by Web browsers during image downloads for users who have graphics turned off, and for users who rely on screen-reading software to convert graphics on the screen to spoken words.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="137287">alternative text</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1806241">альтэрнатыўны тэкст</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1045_765697_1780195"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Text displayed by Web browsers during image downloads for users who have graphics turned off, and for users who rely on screen-reading software to convert graphics on the screen to spoken words.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="765697">ALT text</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1780195">тэкст замяшчэння</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1045_765697_1806241"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Text displayed by Web browsers during image downloads for users who have graphics turned off, and for users who rely on screen-reading software to convert graphics on the screen to spoken words.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="765697">ALT text</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1806241">альтэрнатыўны тэкст</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10450_102839_1574037"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To put new data in the place of other data, usually after conducting a search for the data to be replaced. Text-based applications such as word processors typically include Find and Replace commands.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="102839">replace</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1574037">замяніць</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10451_16349_1573445"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Relating to frequencies within the range of perception by the human ear - from about 15 to 20,000 hertz (cycles per second).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="16349">audio</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1573445">аўдыя</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10459_116136_2182153"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of markup in markup languages. A start tag is the starting element of a tag pair which contains metainformation about some part of the text.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="116136">start tag</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2182153">пачатковы тэг</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1048_188097_2296082"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Anything owned or controlled by a business, tangible or intangible, that has monetary value and was acquired at a measurable cost.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="188097">asset</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296082">актыў</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10482_236960_1573923"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A button that opens Sync Center.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="236960">Open Sync Center</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1573923">Адкрыць цэнтр сінхранізацыі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10486_149827_2296719"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The basic structure of a view. When you create a view, you must first select one of five view types (table, timeline, day/week/month, card, or icon) to determine how information will be arranged and formatted in your new view.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="149827">view type</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296719">тып прадстаўлення</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10498_168444_1864580"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A user who can schedule meetings, send invitations, do all the sharing activities in a meeting, and admit participants from the lobby.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="168444">Organizer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864580">арганізатар сходу</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10498_168444_2326728"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A user who can schedule meetings, send invitations, do all the sharing activities in a meeting, and admit participants from the lobby.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="168444">Organizer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2326728">арганізатар</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10498_168445_1864580"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A user who can schedule meetings, send invitations, do all the sharing activities in a meeting, and admit participants from the lobby.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="168445">organizer</term><t