st of files, or the Internet, either for a particular item or for anything that seems to be of interest.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="385260">browse for</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1769292">аглядаць</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11249_1166159_1573768"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Light that is beyond red in the color spectrum. While the light is not visible to the human eye, infrared transmitters and receivers can send and receive infrared signals.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1166159">infrared light</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1573768">інфрачырвоны</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11249_66343_1573768"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Light that is beyond red in the color spectrum. While the light is not visible to the human eye, infrared transmitters and receivers can send and receive infrared signals.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="66343">infrared</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1573768">інфрачырвоны</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">B