h uses a smaller focus blue-violet 405 nm laser allowing higher precision and storage density. A competitor to Blu-ray Disc.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="318347">AOD</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2189305">HD</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11543_346954_2189305"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The high definition optical disc format which uses a smaller focus blue-violet 405 nm laser allowing higher precision and storage density. A competitor to Blu-ray Disc.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="346954">HD movie</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2189305">HD</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1155_145640_2296501"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A frame that can contain check boxes, toggle buttons, and option buttons on a form, report, or data access page. You use an option group to present alternatives from which the user can select a single option.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="145640">option group</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296501">група пераключальнікаў</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11558_181384_2296550"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A dialog box that displays information about an object in the interface.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="181384">properties page</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296550">старонка ўласцівасцей</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11563_109159_2296614"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A data structure that contains security information associated with a protected object. Security descriptors include information about who owns the object, who can access it and in what way, and what types of access are audited.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="109159">security descriptor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296614">дэскрыптар бяспекі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11567_216558_1791633"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To arrange to receive a product or use a service regularly.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="216558">subscribe</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1791633">падпісацца</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11576_358360_2296702"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of components and services that enable voice, fax, and email messages to be stored in a user's single mailbox. Users can also access their Microsoft Exchange Server 2007 mailbox from a telephone or a computer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="358360">Unified Messaging server role</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296702">роля сервера адзінай сістэмы абмену паведамленнямі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11591_431903_1806339"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To make a record, file, or other data available in the system.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="431903">activate</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1806339">актываваць</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11608_75547_1573841"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A character that separates items in a list.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="75547">list separator</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1573841">раздзяляльнік элементаў спісу</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11629_109242_1772822"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In Windows-based systems, a unique value that identifies a user, group, or computer account within an enterprise. Every account is issued a SID when it is created.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="109242">security ID</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1772822">ідэнтыфікатар бяспекі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11629_109243_1772822"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In Windows-based systems, a unique value that identifies a user, group, or computer account within an enterprise. Every account is issued a SID when it is created.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="109243">SID</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1772822">ідэнтыфікатар бяспекі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11629_109244_1772822"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In Windows-based systems, a unique value that identifies a user, group, or computer account within an enterprise. Every account is issued a SID when it is created.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="109244">security identifier</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1772822">ідэнтыфікатар бяспекі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11636_145393_2296192"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A file that stores information about a connection to a data source, such as an Access database, spreadsheet, or text file, and that facilitates data source administration.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="145393">Office data connection file</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296192">файл падключэння да дадзеных</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11636_145393_2296487"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A file that stores information about a connection to a data source, such as an Access database, spreadsheet, or text file, and that facilitates data source administration.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="145393">Office data connection file</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296487">файл падключэння да дадзеных Office</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11636_266828_2296192"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A file that stores information about a connection to a data source, such as an Access database, spreadsheet, or text file, and that facilitates data source administration.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="266828">data connection file</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296192">файл падключэння да дадзеных</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11636_266828_2296487"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A file that stores information about a connection to a data source, such as an Access database, spreadsheet, or text file, and that facilitates data source administration.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="266828">data connection file</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296487">файл падключэння да дадзеных Office</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11636_652642_2296192"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A file that stores information about a connection to a data source, such as an Access database, spreadsheet, or text file, and that facilitates data source administration.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="652642">ODC file</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296192">файл падключэння да дадзеных</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11636_652642_2296487"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A file that stores information about a connection to a data source, such as an Access database, spreadsheet, or text file, and that facilitates data source administration.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="652642">ODC file</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296487">файл падключэння да дадзеных Office</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11642_370842_1864572"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An Internet protocol used for sending electronic mail.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="370842">mailto</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864572">mailto</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11655_27151_2785709"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A digital video device that is used for recording moving images and audio in a digital format.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="27151">camera</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2785709">камера</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11655_780638_2785709"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A digital video device that is used for recording moving images and audio in a digital format.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="780638">digital video camera</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2785709">камера</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11672_27099_1996259"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A camera for use with a computer to transmit a video picture.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="27099">webcam</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1996259">вэб-камера</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11707_237298_1864505"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that enables the user to create, manage and apply standardized citations and references in a document.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="237298">Reference Builder</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864505">Канструктар спасылак</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11709_86813_2296762"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A program file used to connect to a particular database. Each database program, such as Access or dBASE, or database management system, such as SQL Server, requires a different driver.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="86813">ODBC driver</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296762">драйвер ODBC</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1171_13558_1864083"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A technical article, written and distributed by Microsoft, that provides additional information about a Microsoft product or a fix for a known issue.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="13558">application note</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864083">указанне па ўжыванні</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11712_307435_2296405"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that allows access to SharePoint documents and sites and documents on shares inside of a corporate network through Outlook Web Access when it is used remotely.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="307435">LinkAccess</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296405">LinkAccess</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11717_343653_1770871"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To find.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="343653">locate</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1770871">знайсці</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11727_231965_1864416"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Components that can be installed on your computer to add commands and functions to Excel. These add-in programs are specific to Excel. Other add-in programs that are available for Excel or Office are Component Object Model (COM) add-ins.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="231965">Excel add-in</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864416">Надбудова Excel</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11734_258953_1573738"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A digital interface specification for delivering digital content and connecting consumer electronic devices.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="258953">high-density multichip interconnect</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1573738">HDMI</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11734_258956_1573738"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A digital interface specification for delivering digital content and connecting consumer electronic devices.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="258956">HDMI</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1573738">HDMI</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11734_298004_1573738"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A digital interface specification for delivering digital content and connecting consumer electronic devices.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="298004">high-definition multimedia interface</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1573738">HDMI</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11744_38453_1573564"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A person, inside or outside your organization, for whom you have created an entry where you can save several types of information, such as street and email addresses, telephone and fax numbers, and Web page URLs.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="38453">contact</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1573564">кантакт</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11757_146879_1772802"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The device that communicates between your software program and your printer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="146879">printer driver</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1772802">драйвер прынтара</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11758_153847_2296265"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An object created with one program and embedded into a document created by another. Embedding the object, rather than simply inserting or pasting it, ensures that the object retains its original format. If you double-click the embedded object, you can edit it with the toolbars and menus from the program used to create it.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="153847">embedded object</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296265">убудаваны аб'ект</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11759_307436_2296442"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The mechanism used to help a caller differentiate between users with names that match the touch-tone or speech input.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="307436">Matched Name Selection Method</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296442">Метад выбару імён</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11765_2795839_1574236"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Microsoft's antimalware solution that provides next generation protection for desktops, portable computers, and servers.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2795839">Microsoft Defender Antivirus</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1574236">Абаронца Windows</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11765_3178800_1574236"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Microsoft's antimalware solution that provides next generation protection for desktops, portable computers, and servers.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3178800">Defender Antivirus</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1574236">Абаронца Windows</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11767_140546_1864240"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A file containing data where individual field values are separated by a character, such as a comma or a tab.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="140546">delimited text file</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864240">тэкставы файл з раздзяляльнікамі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11777_64765_1573761"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A tool that lets you enter complex characters and symbols, such as those used in East Asian written languages, using a standard keyboard.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="64765">IME</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1573761">IME</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11777_64765_1864121"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A tool that lets you enter complex characters and symbols, such as those used in East Asian written languages, using a standard keyboard.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="64765">IME</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864121">рэдактар ​​метаду ўводу</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11777_64766_1573761"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A tool that lets you enter complex characters and symbols, such as those used in East Asian written languages, using a standard keyboard.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="64766">input method editor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1573761">IME</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11777_64766_1864121"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A tool that lets you enter complex characters and symbols, such as those used in East Asian written languages, using a standard keyboard.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="64766">input method editor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864121">рэдактар ​​метаду ўводу</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11782_149770_1864347"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A diagram that is used to show areas of overlap between and among elements.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="149770">Venn diagram</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864347">дыяграма Вена</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11795_147980_1574052"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Pertaining to keyboard settings, document views, user interface objects, languages, etc. for which text is displayed in a right-to-left direction.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="147980">right-to-left</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1574052">справа налева</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11795_147980_1806373"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Pertaining to keyboard settings, document views, user interface objects, languages, etc. for which text is displayed in a right-to-left direction.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="147980">right-to-left</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1806373">RTL</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11795_661874_1574052"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Pertaining to keyboard settings, document views, user interface objects, languages, etc. for which text is displayed in a right-to-left direction.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="661874">RTL</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1574052">справа налева</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11795_661874_1806373"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Pertaining to keyboard settings, document views, user interface objects, languages, etc. for which text is displayed in a right-to-left direction.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="661874">RTL</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1806373">RTL</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11797_149448_1864346"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A list that includes the name of the person who originally sent a task request plus the names of everyone who received the task request, reassigned the task to someone else, or chose to keep an updated copy of the task in their task list.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="149448">update list</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864346">спіс абнаўленняў</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11798_106558_2106272"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A line printed above, below, or to the side of some element, either to set that item off from the remainder of the page or to improve the look of the page. Footnotes, for example, often appear below a short rule that sets them off from the main text on the page. The thickness of a rule is typically measured in points. (A point is approximately 1/72 inch.)</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="106558">rule</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2106272">лінейка</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11798_2085540_2106272"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A line printed above, below, or to the side of some element, either to set that item off from the remainder of the page or to improve the look of the page. Footnotes, for example, often appear below a short rule that sets them off from the main text on the page. The thickness of a rule is typically measured in points. (A point is approximately 1/72 inch.)</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2085540">rule line</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2106272">лінейка</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1180_89323_1791115"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To extend over and cover a part of something.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="89323">overlap</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1791115">накладацца</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11800_118815_1660032"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The information about a computer that's derived from the System Information program.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="118815">system info</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1660032">сістэмная інфармацыя</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11803_89506_2308208"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A role that controls how permissions are set and can grant permissions to others.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="89506">owner</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2308208">уладальнік</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11804_118547_1574159"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of entities working together to accomplish a task.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="118547">system</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1574159">сістэма</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11805_121970_1864177"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The slide that stores information from the design template pertaining to styles on title slides, including placeholder sizes and positions, background design, and color schemes.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="121970">title master</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864177">узор тытульнага слайда</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1181_144723_1864293"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Margins of the left page are a mirror image of those of the right page. That is, the inside margins are the same width, and the outside margins are the same width.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="144723">mirror margins</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864293">люстраныя палі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11810_210490_1573665"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A networking standard that uses cables to provide network access. Ethernet is the most widely installed technology for connecting computers.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="210490">Ethernet</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1573665">Ethernet</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11820_125350_1574201"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A character-encoding standard developed by the Unicode Consortium that represents almost all of the written languages of the world. The Unicode character repertoire has multiple representation forms, including UTF-8, UTF-16, and UTF-32. Most Windows interfaces use the UTF-16 form.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="125350">Unicode</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1574201">Юнікод</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11821_77656_1772767"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of display that uses a liquid compound having a polar molecular structure, sandwiched between two transparent electrodes. When an electric field is applied, the molecules align with the field, forming a crystalline arrangement that polarizes the light passing through it. A polarized filter laminated over the electrodes blocks polarized light. In this way, a grid of electrodes can selectively "turn on" a cell, or a pixel, containing the liquid crystal material, turning it dark.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="77656">LCD</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1772767">ВК-манітор</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11821_77658_1772767"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of display that uses a liquid compound having a polar molecular structure, sandwiched between two transparent electrodes. When an electric field is applied, the molecules align with the field, forming a crystalline arrangement that polarizes the light passing through it. A polarized filter laminated over the electrodes blocks polarized light. In this way, a grid of electrodes can selectively "turn on" a cell, or a pixel, containing the liquid crystal material, turning it dark.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="77658">liquid crystal display</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1772767">ВК-манітор</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11832_231956_1864408"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A reference to a range that spans two or more worksheets in a workbook.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="231956">3-D reference</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864408">Аб'ёмная спасылка</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11847_23740_2296112"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A location in a program at which execution is halted so that a programmer can examine the program's status, the contents of variables, and so on.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="23740">breakpoint</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296112">кропка спынення</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11859_1468785_2011587"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A unique bank registration number that a bank uses to identify itself.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1468785">transit number</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2011587">код банка</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11859_1468785_2011596"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A unique bank registration number that a bank uses to identify itself.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1468785">transit number</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2011596">транзітны нумар банка</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11859_1993199_2011587"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A unique bank registration number that a bank uses to identify itself.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1993199">bank transit number</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2011587">код банка</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11859_1993199_2011596"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A unique bank registration number that a bank uses to identify itself.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1993199">bank transit number</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2011596">транзітны нумар банка</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11859_1993209_2011587"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A unique bank registration number that a bank uses to identify itself.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1993209">bank code</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2011587">код банка</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11859_1993209_2011596"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A unique bank registration number that a bank uses to identify itself.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1993209">bank code</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2011596">транзітны нумар банка</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11859_234999_2011587"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A unique bank registration number that a bank uses to identify itself.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="234999">routing number</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2011587">код банка</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11859_234999_2011596"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A unique bank registration number that a bank uses to identify itself.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="234999">routing number</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2011596">транзітны нумар банка</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11859_2898941_2011587"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A unique bank registration number that a bank uses to identify itself.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2898941">bank routing code</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2011587">код банка</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11859_2898941_2011596"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A unique bank registration number that a bank uses to identify itself.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2898941">bank routing code</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2011596">транзітны нумар банка</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11872_51841_1573664"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A keyboard key that sends the escape (ESC) character to the computer. Often this key moves the user back one level in the menu structure or exits the program.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="51841">ESC key</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1573664">клавіша ESC</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11873_94938_1769133"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A customer's right to control how and to what extent their personal information is collected and used and with whom it is shared.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="94938">privacy</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1769133">канфідэнцыйнасць</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11884_123946_2296691"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A logical relationship established between domains to allow pass-through authentication, in which a trusting domain honors the logon authentications of a trusted domain.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="123946">trust relationship</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296691">адносіны даверу</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11886_1995807_2011762"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An identification number that is issued by a tax authority to indicate that a company is not required to pay sales tax.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1995807">exempt ID</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2011762">код звальнення ад падатка</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11886_235021_2011762"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An identification number that is issued by a tax authority to indicate that a company is not required to pay sales tax.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="235021">tax exempt number</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2011762">код звальнення ад падатка</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11893_299914_2072200"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An IP address of the OneNote session that is being shared with other users.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="299914">Shared Address Information</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2072200">сумесны IP-адрас сеанса</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="119_360149_1806325"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An association established between common fields (columns) in two tables. A relationship can be one-to-one, many-to-many, or one-to-many.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="360149">relationship</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1806325">адносіны</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11902_262727_1573955"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that identifies people using computers near you so that you can use features and programs that use peer-to-peer technology.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="262727">People Near Me</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1573955">Суседнія карыстальнікі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11914_39698_1806186"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Any device that changes electrical signals or computer data from one form to another. For example, an analog-to-digital converter translates analog signals to digital signals.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="39698">converter</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1806186">канвертар</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11919_251777_1772808"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A file containing information that the user either requires or will find informative and that might not have been included in the documentation. Readme files are placed on disk in plain-text form (without extraneous or program-specific characters) so that they can be read easily be a variety of word processing programs.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="251777">readme file</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1772808">файл звестак</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11919_251778_1772808"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A file containing information that the user either requires or will find informative and that might not have been included in the documentation. Readme files are placed on disk in plain-text form (without extraneous or program-specific characters) so that they can be read easily be a variety of word processing programs.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="251778">README</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1772808">файл звестак</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11936_23875_1573476"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The amount of light that is emitted by a computer monitor or picture displayed on the monitor.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="23875">brightness</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1573476">яркасць</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11940_298006_1864544"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The application that is used to open an attachment for Attachment Previewing.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="298006">Attachment Previewer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864544">Сродак папярэдняга прагляду далучэнняў</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11947_65138_1573763"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In an environment capable of displaying multiple on-screen windows, any window other than the one currently being used for work. An inactive window can be partially or entirely hidden behind another window, and it remains inactive until the user selects it.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="65138">inactive window</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1573763">неактыўнае акно</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11961_180264_2773869"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A trust relationship between two or more SIP domains that permits users in separate organizations to communicate in real time across network boundaries.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="180264">federation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2773869">федэрацыя</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11983_381857_1864575"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An email folder with associated retention, archive, or expiration policies that are applied to its contents. Organizations can facilitate policy enforcement by providing such folders for users to classify email messages.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="381857">Managed E-mail Folder</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864575">Кіраваная папка электроннай пошты</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR<