rkspaces for managing documents, discussions, lists, surveys and other important contextual information such as team member status and presence.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639899">WSS</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296745">Windows SharePoint Services</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="12540_55239_1864115"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A temporary property of a user-interface object, such as a window, view, dialog box, or button, that permits the object to receive keyboard input from the user. The focus is usually conveyed through highlighting.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="55239">focus</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864115">фокус</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="12548_139813_1806242"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A user dictionary that contains a list of words not in the application dictionary that an author wants the spelling checker to accept as correct.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="139813">custom dictionary</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1806242">персаналiзаваны слоўнiк</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="12551_237304_1864507"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A formula syntax that allows the user to refer to list and pivot data in a friendlier way.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="237304">Structured References</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864507">Структураваныя спасылкі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="12556_361560_1806342"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A classification for grouping content by user-defined criteria such as page contents, file types, or a similar distinction.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="361560">area</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1806342">катэгорыя</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="12556_568110_1806342"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A classification for grouping content by user-defined criteria such as page contents, file types, or a similar distinction.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="568110">category</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1806342">катэгорыя</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="12560_257510_2771593"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An identifier used by two APPC logical units (LUs) to validate security when a session is activated. The security key performs a function similar to that of a password, but at the LU-LU session level rather than at the TP-conversation level.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="257510">security key</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2771593">ключ бяспекі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="12562_232859_1864483"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A stand-alone, dynamic-link library that, when loaded, can add custom commands that extend the functionality of Microsoft Word. Commands and functions in a loaded WLL are also available to Microsoft Visual Basic projects.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="232859">Word Add-in Library</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864483">Бібліятэка WLL</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><ter