n a grid. Vectors are used in the output of some graphics programs instead of groups of dots (on paper) or pixels (on screen).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="127792">vector</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2529787">вектар</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16504_592353_2556687"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A chart that shows a three dimensional surface that connects a set of data points. As in a topographic map, colors and patterns indicate areas that are in the same range of values.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592353">surface chart</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2556687">паверхневая дыяграма</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16505_592354_2764085"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Pertaining to a resource in a failover cluster or server cluster that is in the process of being brought online or offline.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592354">pending</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2764085">чаканне</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16506_592355_1864628"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A surface chart subtype that provides a view of the surface chart from above, with colors representing specific ranges of values.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592355">contour chart</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864628">контурная дыяграма</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16507_592356_1864629"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A contour chart displayed without color.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592356">wireframe contour chart</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864629">бескаляровая контурная дыяграма</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16508_2909978_1864630"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A chart that displays data in rings, where each ring represents a data series.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2909978">donut</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864630">кальцавая дыяграма</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16508_592357_1864630"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A chart that displays data in rings, where each ring represents a data series.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592357">doughnut chart</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864630">кальцавая дыяграма</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16511_592360_1864631"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A doughnut chart that displays the contribution of each value to a total while emphasizing individual values, by showing each slice of the doughnut as "pulled out," or separate, from the whole.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592360">exploded doughnut chart</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864631">разрэзаная кальцавая дыяграма</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16513_592362_1864632"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A best-fit curved trendline that is used when the rate of change in the data increases or decreases quickly and then levels out.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592362">logarithmic trendline</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864632">лагарыфмічная лінія трэнду</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16514_592363_1864633"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A curved trendline that is used when data fluctuates.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592363">polynomial trendline</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864633">полінаміяльная лінія трэнду</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16516_592365_1864634"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A curved trendline that is used with data sets that compare measurements that increase at a specific rate.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592365">power trendline</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864634">ступенная лінія трэнду</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16518_592368_1864635"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A curved trendline that is used when data values rise or fall at constantly increasing rates.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592368">exponential trendline</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864635">экспаненцыяльная лінія трэнду</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16519_592369_1864636"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A trendline that smoothes out fluctuations in data to show a pattern or trend more clearly.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592369">moving average trendline</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864636">лінія трэнду рухомага сярэдняга</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16533_592383_2296717"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A certificate that represents the public-key portion of a token-signing certificate. A verification certificate is stored in the trust policy and used by the federation server in one organization to verify that incoming security tokens have been issued by valid federation servers in the organization's farm and in other organizations.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592383">verification certificate</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296717">сертыфікат праверкі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16577_592433_1806343"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To ensure that all data sources that are used by a KPI or scorecard are available.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592433">validate</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1806343">праверыць</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1658_115875_2296645"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of running a management agent that imports data from a connected data source into the connector space, and then immediately stopping the run.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="115875">staging</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296645">прамежнае захоўванне</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16584_592444_2592198"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A directory name, used in an address, that corresponds to a physical directory on the server.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592444">virtual directory</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2592198">віртуальны каталог</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16594_592578_2182119"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A service or feature that renders the audio content of a television or video program as text on the screen. These captions are usually visible only if decoded or activated.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592578">closed captioning</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2182119">схаваныя субтытры</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16607_592811_1574216"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A numeric or other designation appended to a product name to identify a particular release.​</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592811">version</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1574216">версія</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16609_592813_1772709"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An effect applied to a graphical object that typically reduces the difference between the outline of the object and the graphical area next to it.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592813">blur</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1772709">размытасць</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16612_592816_1791910"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A wireless, mobile device that combines platform software, a browser, a modern chipset, and a telephone handset.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592816">smartphone</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1791910">смартфон</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16612_592837_1791910"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A wireless, mobile device that combines platform software, a browser, a modern chipset, and a telephone handset.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592837">phone</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1791910">смартфон</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16647_594141_1990455"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Software that provides encryption for sensitive data, such as passwords, in applications.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="594141">encryption provider</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1990455">правайдар шыфравання</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16655_594166_2731012"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Information, such as user name and password, for a particular user or account for gaining access to a resource.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="594166">user credentials</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2731012">уліковыя дадзеныя карыстальніка</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16658_600620_1864637"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The round button in the lower left-hand corner of the Windows screen that allows the user to click and display the Start menu.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="600620">Start button</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864637">кнопка "Пуск"</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16665_601385_2626122"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An attack by a malicious user or malicious software on a computer or operating system to find a secret password or a symmetric encryption key by guessing passwords or keys until the correct password or key is discovered.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="601385">key search attack</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2626122">атака метадам падбору</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16665_601386_2626122"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An attack by a malicious user or malicious software on a computer or operating system to find a secret password or a symmetric encryption key by guessing passwords or keys until the correct password or key is discovered.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="601386">brute force attack</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2626122">атака метадам падбору</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1668_147156_1574003"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A grouping of properties presented as a tabbed page of a property sheet.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="147156">property page</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1574003">старонка ўласцівасцей</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16697_601660_1697768"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Microsoft site that provides a comprehensive listing of updates that can be distributed over a corporate network.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="601660">Microsoft Update Catalog</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1697768">Каталог Microsoft Update</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16775_1049762_1754699"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature of Remote Desktop Services that enables the user to access a program remotely through Remote Desktop Services but have it appear as if it is running on the user's local computer. Users can run RemoteApp programs side by side with their local programs.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1049762">RemoteApp</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1754699">RemoteApp</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16775_616468_1754699"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature of Remote Desktop Services that enables the user to access a program remotely through Remote Desktop Services but have it appear as if it is running on the user's local computer. Users can run RemoteApp programs side by side with their local programs.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="616468">Terminal Services RemoteApp</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1754699">RemoteApp</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16775_616469_1754699"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature of Remote Desktop Services that enables the user to access a program remotely through Remote Desktop Services but have it appear as if it is running on the user's local computer. Users can run RemoteApp programs side by side with their local programs.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="616469">TS RemoteApp</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1754699">RemoteApp</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1679_1370400_1806289"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The W3C standard language used for writing XML schema documents.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1370400">XSD</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1806289">XML-схема</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1679_1536620_1806289"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The W3C standard language used for writing XML schema documents.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1536620">XML schema definition language</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1806289">XML-схема</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1679_1536621_1806289"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The W3C standard language used for writing XML schema documents.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1536621">XSDL</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1806289">XML-схема</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1679_257436_1806289"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The W3C standard language used for writing XML schema documents.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="257436">XML schema</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1806289">XML-схема</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16798_616805_1864638"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft implementation of an integrity level. In particular, a protection level, refers to an integrity label that contains only level information, without the additional information traditionally contained within integrity level.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="616805">protection level</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864638">узровень абароны</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1682_114990_1864161"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An array (arrangement of items) in which many of the entries are identical, commonly zero. It is not possible to define precisely when an array is sparse, but it is clear that at some point, usually when about one-third of the array consists of identical entries, it becomes worthwhile to redefine the array.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="114990">sparse array</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864161">разрэджаны масіў</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1686_90627_1770267"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A distinct chunk of text that is indicated by formatting such as indentation, numbering, or a new line.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="90627">paragraph</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1770267">абзац</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1688_74871_1573837"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In word processing, a string of characters displayed or printed in a single horizontal row.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="74871">line</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1573837">радок</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16898_625842_2691611"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A list of employees and all the information related to paying them such as wages, taxes, benefits, and deductions.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="625842">payroll</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2691611">разліковы ліст</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16907_627846_1574135"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The date when a project or task is scheduled to begin.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="627846">begin date</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1574135">дата пачатку</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16907_627847_1574135"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The date when a project or task is scheduled to begin.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="627847">start date</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1574135">дата пачатку</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16924_629472_2296203"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The name automatically assigned to an object by a program or process when the user does not specify an alternative.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="629472">default name</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296203">імя па змаўчанні</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16927_629486_2296215"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A user-defined description of a particular device.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="629486">device name</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296215">імя прылады</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16930_2737154_2755143"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The administrator account that can manage all aspects of the Exchange product.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2737154">Exchange service administrator</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2755143">Адміністратар Exchange</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16930_629571_2755143"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The administrator account that can manage all aspects of the Exchange product.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="629571">Exchange administrator</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2755143">Адміністратар Exchange</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1695_397155_2296276"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A hidden item that contains information about an event sink, information about what events will trigger the event sink, and options that tell when or under what conditions the event sink will be triggered. The event registration item is created in the same folder that is being monitored for events.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="397155">event registration item</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296276">элемент рэгістрацыі падзей</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16957_629941_2296166"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A dialog box in which a user confirms that he or she wants a specified action to occur, usually by clicking OK.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="629941">confirmation dialog box</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296166">дыялогавае акно пацвярджэння</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16960_629944_2296252"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A three-digit string of numbers, such as 5.1.2., that indicates the status of an attempt to deliver an email message.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="629944">DSN code</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296252">код DSN</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16962_629946_2296256"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The value that is applied to a specific DWORD.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="629946">DWORD value</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296256">значэнне DWORD</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16963_629993_1864639"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A unique view for displaying appointments, tasks, and other information in the form of a Web page. You can customize the Outlook Today page for your organization, or for individuals or groups within your organization, to display the information most relevant to them.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="629993">Outlook Today</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864639">Outlook сёння</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="170_502935_1573434"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A part of the user interface dedicated to a particular purpose, such as "instant message area."</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="502935">area</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1573434">вобласць</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1700_122674_1770911"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of viewing and updating the actual progress of tasks so that you can see progress across time, evaluate slippage of tasks, compare scheduled or baseline data to actual data, and check the completion percentage of tasks and your project.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="122674">tracking</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1770911">адсочванне</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1701_130254_1806236"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The programming language designed at Microsoft that was derived from BASIC and that was designed to enable the easy development of visual applications and components in Windows.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="130254">Visual Basic</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1806236">Visual Basic</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1701_370712_1806236"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The programming language designed at Microsoft that was derived from BASIC and that was designed to enable the easy development of visual applications and components in Windows.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="370712">VB</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1806236">Visual Basic</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1703_142906_1778323"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A line added to a chart that makes it easier to view and evaluate data.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="142906">gridline</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1778323">лінія сеткі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17036_2629683_2644761"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft volume licensing contract designed for large companies and government organizations that provides a license grant on a perpetual basis.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2629683">EA</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2644761">Пагадненне Enterprise</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17036_639060_2644761"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft volume licensing contract designed for large companies and government organizations that provides a license grant on a perpetual basis.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="639060">Enterprise Agreement</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2644761">Пагадненне Enterprise</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1706_3257_1574072"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A program that invokes other programs in order to accomplish its tasks.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3257">script</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1574072">сцэнарый</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1707_81769_2296467"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The action of pressing and releasing one of the mouse buttons.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="81769">mouse click</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296467