sing, disk, and printer resources of another computer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1030794">single-user computer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1817047">персанальны камп'ютар</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2400_91272_1817046"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A microcomputer designed for use by one person at a time. Personal computers do not need to share the processing, disk, and printer resources of another computer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="91272">PC</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1817046">ПК</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2400_91272_1817047"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A microcomputer designed for use by one person at a time. Personal computers do not need to share the processing, disk, and printer resources of another computer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="91272">PC</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1817047">персанальны камп'ютар</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2400_91273_1817046"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A microcomputer designed for use by one person at a time. Personal computers do not need to share the processing, disk, and printer resources of another computer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="91273">personal computer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1817046">ПК</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2400_91273_1817047"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A microcomputer designed for use by one person at a time. Personal computers do not need to share the processing, disk, and printer resources of another computer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="91273">personal computer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1817047">персанальны камп'ютар</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24002_1093138_1998032"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A UI or media segment that can display on top of or play concurrently with another UI or media segment.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1093138">overlay</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1998032">накладанне</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24016_1093171_2592488"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A powerful stand-alone computer of the sort used in computer-aided design and other applications requiring a high-end, usually expensive, machine with considerable calculating or graphics capability.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1093171">workstation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2592488">працоўная станцыя</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24039_1097320_2641203"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">On retailer websites, a collection of desired products or items a customer saves to their user account for future reference.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1097320">wish list</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2641203">спіс пажаданняў</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24043_1097333_2515428"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Software that provides a common application programming interface (API). Applications written using that API will run in the same computer systems as the middleware.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1097333">middleware</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2515428">сувязнае праграмнае забеспячэнне</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2405_2020064_2021413"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The amount of battery power left on the system.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2020064">battery level</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2021413">зарад акумулятара</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2405_2020064_2021414"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The amount of battery power left on the system.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2020064">battery level</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2021414">узровень акумулятара</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2405_236972_2021413"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The amount of battery power left on the system.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="236972">battery charge</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2021413">зарад акумулятара</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2405_236972_2021414"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The amount of battery power left on the system.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="236972">battery charge</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2021414">узровень акумулятара</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24051_1097914_2028986"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To return to a stable condition after some error has occurred. A program recovers from an error by stabilizing itself and resuming execution of instructions without user intervention.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1097914">recover</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2028986">аднавіцца</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24057_1098418_1864886"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A collection of statistics that indicates the degree to which a service meets performance, usage, and other demands for the service.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1098418">service quality metrics</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864886">паказчыкі якасці абслугоўвання</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2407_73729_1770864"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In programming, the order and sequence of input and output.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="73729">layout</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1770864">структура</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24076_1098449_2689575"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The time during which a program is running. In most interactive programs, a session is the time during which the program accepts input and processes information.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1098449">session</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2689575">сеанс</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24102_1098534_1864887"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feed that provides users with information, notifications and updates based on people, documents, and tags they are following.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1098534">activity feed</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864887">вэб-канал актыўнасці</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24102_1098534_1865119"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feed that provides users with information, notifications and updates based on people, documents, and tags they are following.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1098534">activity feed</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1865119">пакет навін</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termN