ions. You create a new section when you want to change such properties as line numbering, number of columns, or headers and footers.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="232848">section</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1574082">секцыя</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6700_232840_1864471"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Formatting applied to a heading. Microsoft Office Word has nine different built-in styles: Heading 1 through Heading 9.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="232840">heading style</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1864471">стыль загалоўка</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6703_397177_2296426"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A mail-enabled Active Directory user object that has mailbox attributes.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="397177">mailbox user</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296426">карыстальнік паштовай скрынкі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6707_307425_2296273"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A zone of non-communication between distinct departments of a business or organization to prevent conflicts of interest that might result in the inappropriate release of sensitive information.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="307425">ethical wall</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2296273">абмежаванне ў адпаведнасці з карпаратыўнымі стандартамі</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6708_29444_1573515"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To align objects or text around a point located in the middle of a line, page, or other defined area; in effect, to position items an equal distance from each margin or border.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="29444">center</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1573515">цэнтраваць</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6711_251891_2687256"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To give a unique cardinal position to each entry, as in stack rank.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="251891">rank</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2687256">ранжыраваць</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6711_542928_2687256"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To give a unique cardinal position to each entry, as in stack rank.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="542928">prioritize</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2687256">ранжыраваць</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6714_159462_1816148"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that allows for automatic forwarding of incoming calls.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="159462">call forwarding</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="be"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1816148">пераадрасацыя выклікаў</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">BLR</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6718_78054_1864131"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A nonprinting mark you insert to end the current line and continue the text on the 